          "source_quote": "τῆς αὐτοῦ ἐπακούων ὁμιλίας",
          "english_quote": "and heeding his discourse.",
          "issue": "The possessive αὐτοῦ most naturally refers to the presiding leader, but its relationship to the unresolved preceding αὐτόν remains uncertain. The draft preserves the pronoun and discloses the alternative; it does not establish whose discourse is heeded. This separately disclosed blocking issue cannot be cleared merely by retaining neutral English.",
          "suggested_revision": "Provide a separate antecedent analysis using the supplied paragraph, including the recurring references to the leader and the preceding reconciliation clause. Preserve the alternative if the evidence remains inconclusive. No correction to the Greek is presently justified, and the passage remains blocked.",
